{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>And the livestock of the Levites, etc.</b> — meaning, the animals that they are obligated in redemption, namely the firstborn of donkeys, for Scripture says (Exodus 13:13) ״וּפֶטֶר חֲמוֹר תִּפְדֶּה בְשֶׂה״, and specifically the firstborn of a donkey, but not firstborn of clean animals, for unblemished ones are not subject to redemption, and blemished ones — from the moment they become blemished, for one instant they are in the owners' domain, the firstborn acquires title to it and it is in his possession like unconsecrated property, so what room is there for redemption?"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The parenthetical (הַבְּכוֹר) appears in the source; I translate it as 'the firstborn' integrated into the sentence."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:05:57.181674522Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}